          "item": "https://www.patronaccounting.com/trademark-search-report/delhi"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I search trademarks online from Delhi for free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. The IP India Public Search at tmrsearch.ipindia.gov.in is free with no login. You can search by wordmark, phonetic similarity, Vienna Code, application number, or proprietor. However, it provides raw data without analysis. Patron adds multi-variant methodology, phonetic analysis, status verification, and a legal registrability opinion."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is trademark search mandatory before filing in Delhi?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. The Act doesn't require pre-filing search. However, filing without search dramatically increases Section 11 objection risk, delaying registration by 6-12+ months. A professional search costs Rs 1,999-4,999 versus Rs 4,500-9,000 in wasted fees. For Delhi's competitive market, search is commercially essential."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is a phonetic search and why does it matter?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Phonetic search identifies marks that sound similar regardless of spelling. 'Kwik Kleen' sounds like 'Quick Clean'. Examiners evaluate phonetic similarity under Section 11. A mark passing exact-text search may still be cited against a phonetically similar mark. Patron's analysis catches these hidden conflicts."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a professional search report take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Basic wordmark: 1-2 hours. Comprehensive single-class: 4-6 hours. Multi-class: 6-12 hours. Extended with domain/MCA: 12-24 hours. Portfolio searches: 1-3 days. Turnaround calibrated to Delhi business decision timelines."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What does the search report include?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Complete list of conflicts with trademark name, registration number, class, proprietor, status. Similarity analysis for each. Status verification. GREEN/AMBER/RED risk rating per conflict and overall registrability opinion. Recommended next steps for Delhi businesses."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a clean search guarantee registration?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. A clean search significantly reduces risk but doesn't guarantee. Examiner may identify new applications filed after your search, interpret similarity differently, or raise Section 9 objections. However, professional search eliminates the most common objection cause - Section 11 citation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should I search in multiple Nice classes?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, if your Delhi business spans multiple categories. A D2C brand selling online needs the product class AND Class 35 for online retail. Well-known marks are protected across all 45 classes under Section 11(2). Patron maps all relevant classes based on actual and planned activities."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens if the search finds conflicts?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Options: modify the proposed mark, file in a different class, proceed with awareness preparing for Section 11 objection reply, or choose an entirely different name. Patron advises on the most commercially sensible option based on conflict risk level."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
