<!-- SECTION 15A: LEGAL FRAMEWORK -->
<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal Framework for Trademark Search</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Search Portal:</strong> <a href="https://tmrsearch.ipindia.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IP India Public Search</a> - free, no login, covers all registered and pending marks.</p><p><strong>Classification:</strong> Nice Classification (45 classes). Correct class selection critical for accurate search.</p><p><strong>Section 11 Risk:</strong> Registrar refuses marks identical/similar to existing marks for same/similar goods. Section 11(2) protects well-known marks across all classes.</p><p><strong>Section 9 Risk:</strong> Descriptive, non-distinctive, generic marks refused regardless of search results.</p><p><strong>Not Mandatory But Essential:</strong> No statutory requirement for pre-filing search, but large percentage of applications receive Section 11 objections that could have been anticipated.</p><p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://ipindia.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ipindia.gov.in</a></p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

